/*
 * Declares the BlockValue class.
 *
 * BlockValue represents a lexical block in the generator IR. A block is a
 * sequence of generator values evaluated in order, where the last value
 * determines the value of the block unless `noValue` is set. Blocks introduce a
 * scope that defines the lifetime of variables declared inside them, unless the
 * block is marked as a “set block” (`isSet`), in which case it reuses the
 * parent scope.
 *
 * BlockValue also aggregates control-flow metadata such as break and return
 * locations, and collects throwers from all contained values.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::scope::block
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/scope/block.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *   - Emile Cadorel <emile.cadorel@davidson.fr>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-12-06
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
